# Fixed 2026-10-08, defect 474, lane b15-check (class improvement).
# Symptom: a function type nested n deep in a signature made the checker
# copy the type table's entries as the square of n: 41,050 at 250, 143,925
# at 500.
# Cause: `check/table.intern` pushed each new type through the table's own
# field, `t.nodes @ t.nodes.push(ty)`, which copies every type before it:
# defect 409's shape, repaired in lane b14-p409 (`table.append_node`), on
# which this shape copies 806 and 959.
# This case: the shape at 500, 500 function types interned one inside the
# next, and one mistake beside them, told once.

